input.prompt:
You are the DATA fork. Write and run `frontend/scripts/drkg_scene.py` (numpy only, no sklearn) that turns the raw DRKG release into the static files the 3D scene reads. Another fork is building the scene against the exact format below in parallel, so DO NOT change the format; if something truly can't be produced, fill it with null and tell me.

Inputs (gitignored, in `data/raw/drkg/` of this worktree; my background download may still be finishing — the tarball was ~176/207 MB at handoff and gets extracted in place. If `embed/DRKG_TransE_l2_entity.npy` isn't there yet, write the script first; check again; the tar may extract to `./drkg.tsv`, `./embed/...`, `./relation_glossary.tsv`. If the download failed, re-run: `curl -fLsS --retry 2 -o data/raw/drkg/drkg.tar.gz https://dgl-data.s3-us-west-2.amazonaws.com/dataset/DRKG/drkg.tar.gz` then `tar -xzf`). Also `data/raw/drkg/hetionet-v1.0-nodes.tsv` (id like `Gene::3480`, name = symbol; `Compound::DB00026` etc.). Extra compound names: `git show origin/cursor/pipeline-graph-ui:data/kg_scores.json` (`compounds[].drkg_id` / `.name`, DrugCentral names).

Outputs in `frontend/public/drkg/`:
1. `points.bin` — little-endian Float32, 3·N, N=97,238, entity row order of `embed/entities.tsv`. P(x) = ((x − μ)·W)·s, W = top-3 principal axes (eigh of the 400×400 covariance), μ = mean entity vector, s so the 98th-percentile radius = 10. Query vectors use the SAME P, so P(e−r) = P(e) − s·(r·W): translation arrows are exact.
2. `types.bin` — Uint8, N values, index into `scene.json.types`.
3. `names.json` — `{ "<row>": "label" }` for every entity with a known human label (Hetionet names + kg_scores DrugCentral names; ALS = "Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis"). Hover only. Keep it under ~1 MB (round nothing, just labels).
4. `scene.json`:
```ts
type Vec3 = [number, number, number] // round to 3 decimals
type Scene = {
  meta: { model: string /* "DRKG pretrained TransE_l2, 400d" */; entities: number; projection: string /* "PCA-3, global, numpy" */;
          explainedVariance: [number, number, number]; relation: string /* "DRUGBANK::target::Compound:Gene" */;
          formula: string /* "q = e[gene] − r[target]; d(c) = ‖e[c] − q‖₂ in 400-d; profile distance = min over its genes" */;
          universe: number /* count of Compound::DB\d{5} searched */; topK: number /* 5 */ }
  types: { name: string; count: number }[]   // index = types.bin value; sorted by count desc
  als: { id: string; row: number; pos: Vec3; label: string }   // Disease::MESH:D000690
  profiles: {
    lane: number; name: string
    genes: { symbol: string; id: string; row: number; pos: Vec3; query: Vec3 /* P(e[gene] − r) */;
             targetEdges: number /* real compound–gene edges on this gene, all compound–gene relations */;
             alsEdge: string | null /* relation name of a DRKG gene–ALS edge (either direction), else null */ }[]
    unresolved: string[]   // targets that didn't resolve to a Gene node / vector
    matches: { rank: number; id: string; row: number; name: string; pos: Vec3; distance: number /* true 400-d L2, 3 dp */;
               viaGene: string; directEdge: boolean /* DRKG has a compound–viaGene edge */ }[]  // top-5 ascending
    edges: { from: number; to: number; rel: string }[]   // real DRKG edges as rows, gene → compound; cap ~24 per gene: matches first, then named compounds
  }[]
  handWritten: { drug: string; lane: number; source: 'MATCHES' | 'CANDIDATES'; id: string | null; rank: number | null; distance: number | null }[]
}
```
Params (decided, log-worthy): profiles = Jeremy's five `PROFILES` in `frontend/src/lib/pipeline.ts`; strip parentheticals ("RET (GDNF)" → RET, "SLC1A2 (EAAT2)" → SLC1A2, "NTRK2 (BDNF)" → NTRK2, "NFE2L2 (NRF2)" → NFE2L2); resolve symbol → `Gene::<Entrez>` via Hetionet names (verify, don't guess Entrez ids). Relation `DRUGBANK::target::Compound:Gene`. Universe = entities matching `Compound::DB\d{5}`. Compound–gene edges = every relation whose type pair is Compound:Gene or Gene:Compound (one streaming pass over drkg.tsv; also collect gene–ALS edges in that pass). handWritten = every drug in `MATCHES` and `CANDIDATES` from pipeline.ts, resolved to DrugBank ids via names (Hetionet/kg_scores, case-insensitive) — mark null if absent; rank/distance within its own lane's profile.

Leave one runnable check inside the script (asserts at the end, per AGENTS.md): e.g. the projected query equals P(e) − s·(r·W) to 1e-4, and that a compound with a known DRUGBANK::target edge to a profile gene (e.g. tocilizumab→IL6R if present) ranks in the top few hundred for that gene's query. Print explained variance, per-profile top-5 (name, distance, viaGene, directEdge), unresolved genes, the handWritten landings, output file sizes, runtime.

Do not touch any other file. Do not commit (I'll commit). Final report to me: the printed summary above verbatim (it's the blocker evidence I need to show the user), the exact command to rerun, and anything you had to deviate on.

